      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Modern historians generally view the UN's effectiveness as highly mixed and often deeply qualified. While the organization has successfully mediated and provided humanitarian aid in numerous crises, its power to prevent major, large-scale conflicts is frequently limited by the veto power of its permanent Security Council members. Consequently, many scholars argue the UN is better described as a forum for conflict management and humanitarian response rather than a definitive conflict prevention mechanism.",
