    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "right, so it's a bit of a deadlock then. but looking at recent history, like the stuff in ukraine or syria, does it feel like there's still a real case for the UN being the main way to handle these things? or are people starting to see the 'multilateral' approach as just a way for big countries to mask their own agendas while the system stays stuck?",
